<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bagratuni dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bagratids of Armenia, Bagratids (Armenia), Armenian Bagratids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bagratuni dynasty was an Armenian noble house that rose from among the great princely families of the Arsacid kingdom to become the leading power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. Ashot I was recognised as king in 884–885 by both the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> and the Byzantine emperor, and the dynasty ruled the restored Kingdom of Armenia, from Ani in its later years, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> annexed it in 1045.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bagratuni-dynasty.jpg" alt="Bagratuni dynasty" width="320" height="537" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagratunis_symbol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
